Guard PipeWire stream format positions against unfilled node data

The port count and the channel-position array of a node arrive on
different PipeWire events: m_sinks/m_sources grow as port registry
events come in, while m_position_codes is only filled when a later
Format param event lands on the node.  stream_sink_open() and
stream_source_open() indexed the vector by the port count with no
bound: caught between the two events, the vector is empty, data() of
an empty vector is null, and the read is a null dereference.

On the appliance this crashed the emulator at startup several times in
a row, timing-dependent enough that whether stdout was a pipe or
/dev/null decided whether it survived - which is what a two-event race
looks like from the outside.  Missing entries now fall back to
SPA_AUDIO_CHANNEL_UNKNOWN, and the loop is also clamped to
SPA_AUDIO_MAX_CHANNELS, the size of the fixed position array it fills.

--- a/src/osd/modules/sound/pipewire_sound.cpp
+++ b/src/osd/modules/sound/pipewire_sound.cpp
@@ -805,8 +805,16 @@
 		rate,
 		stream.m_channels
 	};
-	for(uint32_t i=0; i != snode.m_sinks; i++)
-		format.position[i] = snode.m_position_codes[i];
+	// The port count and the position array arrive on different events:
+	// m_sinks grows as port registry events come in, m_position_codes is
+	// filled by a later Format param event on the node.  Between the two,
+	// the vector is still empty - and data() of an empty vector is null,
+	// so indexing it is a null dereference, not garbage.  Seen in the
+	// wild as a startup segfault on the appliance, timing-dependent
+	// enough that redirecting stdout decided whether it crashed.
+	for(uint32_t i=0; i != snode.m_sinks && i != SPA_AUDIO_MAX_CHANNELS; i++)
+		format.position[i] = i < snode.m_position_codes.size()
+			? snode.m_position_codes[i] : SPA_AUDIO_CHANNEL_UNKNOWN;
 
 	uint8_t buffer[1024];
 	spa_pod_builder b = SPA_POD_BUILDER_INIT(buffer, sizeof(buffer));
@@ -858,8 +866,11 @@
 		rate,
 		stream.m_channels
 	};
-	for(uint32_t i=0; i != snode.m_sources; i++)
-		format.position[i] = snode.m_position_codes[i];
+	// Same guard as the sink side: the position array may not have
+	// arrived yet, and an empty vector's data() is null.
+	for(uint32_t i=0; i != snode.m_sources && i != SPA_AUDIO_MAX_CHANNELS; i++)
+		format.position[i] = i < snode.m_position_codes.size()
+			? snode.m_position_codes[i] : SPA_AUDIO_CHANNEL_UNKNOWN;
 
 	uint8_t buffer[1024];
 	spa_pod_builder b = SPA_POD_BUILDER_INIT(buffer, sizeof(buffer));
